.SH NAME
CWE\-1287 \- Improper Validation of Specified Type of Input
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product receives input that is expected to be of a certain type, but it does not validate or incorrectly validates that the input is actually of the expected type. When input does not comply with the expected type, attackers could trigger unexpected errors, cause incorrect actions to take place, or exploit latent vulnerabilities that would not be possible if the input conformed with the expected type. This weakness can appear in type\-unsafe programming languages, or in programming languages that support casting or conversion of an input to another type.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB1\fR exploited CVE mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2024\-4879
ServiceNow Utah, Vancouver, and Washington DC Now Platform, added 2024\-07\-29.
.PP
ServiceNow Improper Input Validation Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
ServiceNow Utah, Vancouver, and Washington DC Now Platform releases contain a jelly template injection vulnerability in UI macros. An unauthenticated user could exploit this vulnerability to execute code remotely.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply mitigations per vendor instructions, or discontinue use.
 Due 2024\-08\-19.
.PP
